  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_che_a20.png\">\r\n\r\n$2-R, 3-R$ configuration, s0 it is a chiral compound<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_che_a20a.png\">\r\n\r\n$2-R, 3-S$ configuration has plane of symmetry or in other words, rotation of hall part is cancelled by the other half, so it is not a chiral compound.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_che_a20b.png\">\r\n\r\n$2-S, 3-S$ configuration, so it is also a chiral compound.",
